     from Apache FOP 2.11: a test of hook page-number-restart (fop/CR-017.2). -->
<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      fox:page-number-restart on a part of a page-sequence that starts part-way down a page, in the four shapes
      Word was probed in (docx4j CR-031, P3, P6, P7). The page the part starts on prints its owner's number. The
      part's count begins on that page; with fox:page-number-restart-parity="keep" (odd and even headers), only
      if the restart number has that page's parity, else on the next page. First sequence (P3): restart at 1
      from part-way down page 2, no parity: 1, 2, 2, 3. Second (P6): the same with parity kept: 1, 2, 1, 2, 3.
      Third (P7): restart at 2, parity kept: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. Fourth (P7): restart at 1 from part-way down page 1,
      parity kept: 1, 2, 3, 4.
    </p>
  </info>
